# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Tailoring --out` from Forever's client tables, trainer lists and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/tailoring
title Tailoring 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Tailoring sews cloth into bolts and the bolts into cloth armour, bags and shirts. It needs no
# gathering profession: humanoids drop the cloth of their level as you quest. Thread and dyes come
# from tailoring and trade supplies vendors.
#
# Forever's changes: nearly every pattern moved 25 points down: trainers teach it 25 points earlier
# (Bolt of Silk Cloth at 100, Gloves of Meditation at 105) and it greys sooner. Forever adds school
# sets (sashes, slippers, belts and more), reagent bags, and the Faction Banner camp item. 74
# patterns need a Spinning Wheel, a camp station (skill 140) from a blueprint the Unstable Sentinel
# drops in the City of Dalaran; 43 more need the skill-300 Loom (no known source); Mooncloth needs a
# Moonwell. New patterns are also sold for Merchant's Favor by Jim'bek near the Crossroads and Mivin
# Shadowweave at Three Corners (Redridge). Merchant's Favor is a currency from the supply crates
# turned in at the camps, not gold; its patterns bind when picked up. Tailoring has no
# specialisation on Forever.
#
# Ranks: Journeyman needs character level 10 (Forever's sniffed lists). Expert is taught only by
# Georgio Bolero (Stormwind) and Josef Gregorian (Undercity), plus the Artisan trainers Timothy
# Worthington (Theramore, Dustwallow Marsh) and Daryl Stack (Tarren Mill, Hillsbrad).
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-15  Linen Cloak, about 7 (known): 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread each
#    15-75  Linen Belt, about 65 (trainer 50c): 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread each
#    75-104 Woolen Cape, about 42 (trainer 2s 50c): 1 Bolt of Woolen Cloth and 1 Fine Thread each
#   104-135 Stylish Red Shirt, about 49 (trainer 2s 50c): 3 Bolt of Woolen Cloth, 2 Red Dye and 1 Fine Thread each
#   135-150 Formal White Shirt, about 17 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Bleach and 1 Fine Thread each
#   150-170 Azure Silk Cloak, about 22 (recipe 15s): 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Blue Dye and 2 Fine Thread each
#   170-197 Black Mageweave Vest, about 30 (trainer): 2 Bolt of Mageweave and 3 Silken Thread each
#   197-225 Black Mageweave Headband, about 40 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Mageweave and 2 Heavy Silken Thread each
#   225-234 Runecloth Belt, about 11 (trainer): 3 Bolt of Runecloth and 1 Rune Thread each
#   234-265 Runecloth Gloves, about 43 (recipe 1g 60s): 4 Bolt of Runecloth, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread each
#   265-300 Runecloth Shoulders, about 62 (pattern from the Auction House): 7 Bolt of Runecloth, 2 Ironweb Spider Silk, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, recipes 50c, vendor goods 7s 20c; gather or buy 144 Linen Cloth.
# 75-150: Journeyman 5s, recipes 11s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 1g 65s 50c; gather
# or buy 567 Wool Cloth and 204 Silk Cloth.
# 150-225: recipes 15s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 21g 16s; gather or buy 264 Silk
# Cloth and 900 Mageweave Cloth.
# 225-300: recipes 1g 60s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor goods 58g; gather or buy 420 Rugged
# Leather, 3195 Runecloth and 124 Ironweb Spider Silk.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# ASSUMED: learn skills of Formal White Shirt 135, Bolt of Mageweave 140, Black Mageweave Vest 170,
# Black Mageweave Headband 190, Bolt of Runecloth 205 and Runecloth Belt 210 (no sniffed Forever
# list teaches them: Classic's trainer skill moved as far as Forever moved the recipe's colours,
# which the sniffed lists bear out on 126 of 129 recipes). In-game check: the skill the trainer
# asks; their prices are not in the data.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed lists ask level 1
# for Apprentice and 10 for Journeyman). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Tailoring 1-75

step Learn Tailoring
  tip Apprentice Tailoring lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Any Tailoring trainer of your faction teaches it; the arrow picks the nearest. Keep every Linen Cloth you loot: humanoids of level 5-20 drop it. 1-75 takes about 50c of recipes and 7s 20c of vendor goods, plus 144 Linen Cloth to gather or buy.
  train Tailoring Apprentice
  skill Tailoring 1

step Tailoring 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 72 Coarse Thread (7s 20c); about 7s 20c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2320 x72 nearest

step Linen Cloth
  tip 144 Linen Cloth for Linen Cloak and Linen Belt: humanoids of level 5-20 drop it; or the Auction House. The arrow picks a farm spot for your level and faction.
  collect 2589 x144 nearest

step Linen Cloak to 15
  tip Linen Cloak is orange at 1 (yellow 35, green 47, grey 60): about 7 crafts to 15, a point every craft. Each takes 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread. Make the 7 Bolt of Linen Cloth first: it gives points too while not grey. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data.
  craft 2963 x7
  craft 2387 until 15

step Tailoring recipes at 15
  tip Back to a Tailoring trainer: Linen Belt (from 15, 50c).
  learn 8776

step Linen Belt to 75
  tip Linen Belt is orange at 15 (yellow 50, green 67, grey 85): about 65 crafts to 75. Each takes 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread. Make the 65 Bolt of Linen Cloth first: it gives points too while not grey. Each belt takes one bolt; the belts sell to vendors.
  craft 2963 x65
  craft 8776 until 75
  skill Tailoring 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman (75-150)
section Tailoring 75-150

step Journeyman Tailoring
  tip Journeyman raises the cap from 75 to 150 for 5s; it needs Tailoring 50 and character level 10, so you can take it on any visit from 50. Not every Tailoring trainer teaches it: Alliance Georgio Bolero (Stormwind City), Grarnik Goodstitch (Stranglethorn Vale), Jormund Stonebrow (Ironforge), Me'lynn (Darnassus), Othesia Evengale (Zephras Isle), Sellandus (Stormwind City), Taleen Shimmerthread (Zephras Isle) and Timothy Worthington (Dustwallow Marsh); Horde Daryl Stack (Hillsbrad Foothills), Grarnik Goodstitch (Stranglethorn Vale), Josef Gregorian (Undercity), Magar (Orgrimmar), Mahani (The Barrens), Othesia Evengale (Zephras Isle), Rhiannon Davis (Undercity), Taleen Shimmerthread (Zephras Isle) and Tepa (Thunder Bluff). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Bolt of Woolen Cloth (from 55, 1s) and Woolen Cape (from 55, 2s 50c). Also learn Faction Banner (1s): Forever's Tailoring camp item, a Bolt of Linen Cloth and a Coarse Thread; each faction has its own. The Camping 101: Tailoring quest from your starting area's camping guide (after The Great Outdoors) sends you to a tailoring trainer who teaches it free. 75-150 takes about 11s of recipes and 1g 65s 50c of vendor goods, plus 567 Wool Cloth and 204 Silk Cloth to gather or buy.
  level 10
  train Tailoring Journeyman
  learn 2964
  learn 2402
  learn 1263425 only Alliance
  learn 1229504 only Horde

step Tailoring 75-150: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 108 Fine Thread (1g 8s), 34 Bleach (8s 50c) and 98 Red Dye (49s); about 1g 65s 50c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 2321 x108 nearest
  buy 2324 x34 nearest
  buy 2604 x98 nearest

