# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Tailoring 225-300

step Artisan Tailoring
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300; it needs Tailoring 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Timothy Worthington (Dustwallow Marsh); Horde Daryl Stack (Hillsbrad Foothills). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Bolt of Runecloth (from 205) and Runecloth Belt (from 210). 225-300 takes about 1g 60s of recipes and 58g of vendor goods, plus 420 Rugged Leather, 3195 Runecloth and 124 Ironweb Spider Silk to gather or buy.
  level 35
  train Tailoring Artisan
  learn 18401
  learn 18402

step Tailoring 225-300: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 116 Rune Thread (58g); about 58g in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra).
  buy 14341 x116 nearest

step Pattern: Runecloth Gloves
  tip Pattern: Runecloth Gloves teaches Runecloth Gloves (Tailoring 230) for 1g 60s. Sold by Qia (Winterspring), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 14481 nearest

