  craft 18402 until 234

step Runecloth Gloves to 265
  tip Runecloth Gloves is orange at 234 (yellow 245, green 260, grey 275): about 43 crafts to 265. Each takes 4 Bolt of Runecloth, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread. Make the 172 Bolt of Runecloth first. Qia in Everlook keeps one pattern at a time; the Timbermaw Hold tunnel from Felwood is the road in, so never kill Timbermaw furbolgs on the way.
  learn 18417 -- from the recipe in your bags
  craft 18401 x172
  craft 18417 until 265

step Runecloth Shoulders to 300
  tip Runecloth Shoulders is orange at 265 (yellow 275, green 290, grey 305): about 62 crafts to 300. Each takes 7 Bolt of Runecloth, 2 Ironweb Spider Silk, 4 Rugged Leather and 1 Rune Thread. Make the 434 Bolt of Runecloth first. Its pattern (Pattern: Runecloth Shoulders) drops from mobs all over the world and does not bind: buy it at the Auction House. Seven bolts, two Ironweb Spider Silk and four Rugged Leather a craft: the dearest stretch. The spiders of Western Plaguelands and Silithus drop the silk (the marked spots), or the Auction House. No pattern on the Auction House? Runecloth Gloves still give a point now and then to 275, and Runecloth Boots (Darnall, Moonglade) to 280, at 4 bolts a craft. Mooncloth (pattern from Qia or Evie Whirlbrew in Everlook; 2 Felcloth at a Moonwell) stays orange to 270 and yellow to 285, but it can be made once every four days. The Spinning Wheel patterns (Merchant's Favor sandals and waistcords from Jim'bek or Mivin Shadowweave; the wheel's blueprint drops from the Unstable Sentinel in the City of Dalaran) and Runecloth Cuffs (Pexmit in Mount Hyjal, 10g; we could not confirm that vendor yet) are the other ways on. Tailoring 300 is a Legacy System milestone.
  learn 18449 -- from the pattern bought at the Auction House
  craft 18401 x434
  craft 18449 until 300
  skill Tailoring 300
